{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01970",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.86,
      "end_seconds": 7.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.78,
      "end_seconds": 13.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "So, you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.65,
      "end_seconds": 28.73,
      "duration_seconds": 14.08,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a barking cough. I don't know what's causing it. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.25,
      "end_seconds": 34.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.24,
      "end_seconds": 44.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.21,
      "end_seconds": 69.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 71, pressure 108 over 73, temperature is 36.7 degrees. And SpO2 97 percent on room air, respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.61,
      "end_seconds": 73.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.92,
      "end_seconds": 80.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon. Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.9,
      "end_seconds": 95.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "It's been about three months now. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.68,
      "end_seconds": 109.26,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.69,
      "end_seconds": 120.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Steamy bathroom helps a bit. A seven out of ten, I suppose. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.06,
      "end_seconds": 124.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.8,
      "end_seconds": 133.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "It usually comes with a hoarse voice. The hoarse voice? That's been for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.99,
      "end_seconds": 157.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Did you get drooling, noisy breathing when resting or difficulty swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.23,
      "end_seconds": 161.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.97,
      "end_seconds": 167.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.98,
      "end_seconds": 170.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.76,
      "end_seconds": 179.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.88,
      "end_seconds": 181.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "No, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.83,
      "end_seconds": 196.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.35,
      "end_seconds": 201.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.18,
      "end_seconds": 206.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.53,
      "end_seconds": 210.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.99,
      "end_seconds": 226.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.3,
      "end_seconds": 231.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Okay, so not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.9,
      "end_seconds": 235.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.41,
      "end_seconds": 238.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.07,
      "end_seconds": 243.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.27,
      "end_seconds": 246.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.6,
      "end_seconds": 267.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "He is playful, breathing comfortably at rest, and I can't hear any noisy breathing now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.04,
      "end_seconds": 272.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.18,
      "end_seconds": 293.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, the most likely explanation is mild croup."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.28,
      "end_seconds": 297.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.21,
      "end_seconds": 314.46,
      "duration_seconds": 15.25,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's mild croup, and we'll watch how it goes. So, to recap quickly. You've had a barking cough for about three months, and no difficulty swallowing or drooling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.48,
      "end_seconds": 317.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.04,
      "end_seconds": 325.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "The treatment will be dexamethasone, 0.15 mg per kg, once, single dose. It's for croup."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.92,
      "end_seconds": 328.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Should I take that with food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.77,
      "end_seconds": 344.88,
      "duration_seconds": 14.11,
      "text": "Keep him calm, sit him upright, and give fluids. Do get help quickly if he makes a noisy sound when resting or struggles to breathe. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.61,
      "end_seconds": 347.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.83,
      "end_seconds": 351.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}